settings-terminal-login-shell = Give programs the environment of my login shell
settings-terminal-login-shell-about = Runs, language servers, plug-in tool windows and the terminal get the variables your login shell sets (PATH, KUBECONFIG, tool folders), read once when the IDE starts, as if they were started from your terminal. A run configuration's own environment variables still win. Turning it off takes effect at once; turning it on, at the next start.
settings-terminal-agents = AI Agents
settings-terminal-agents-about = After a restart a terminal tab resumes the conversation of the AI agent that ran in it, when an adapter knows the agent and the agent reported its conversation id. Plug-ins bring adapters for Claude Code, Codex and Qwen Code; add one here for another agent. Each agent reports its id with a session-start hook that runs the command shown under it (the guide says where each agent keeps its hooks).
